lometres Race Walk, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000785"} "High Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000790"} "Pole Vault, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031120"} "Long Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031134"} "Triple Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000829"} "Shot Put, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000846"} "Discus Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000863"} "Hammer Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000880"} "Javelin Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000897"} "Heptathlon, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000947"} "4 × 400 metres Relay, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "56970"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "57228"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "57515"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "57843"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "58080"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "58376"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "58715"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "59089"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "59475"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "59906"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "60318"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "60814"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "61311"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "61885"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "62432"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "62947"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "63590"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "64272"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "64951"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "65610"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "66290"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257423"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "302536"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "358863"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013751"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/93"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Decathlon, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "4 –  5 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2106"} "Japan National Stadium, Kasumigaoka, Shinjuku, Tokyo"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19000594"} "23 from 15 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Scoring by 1985 point tables."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Defending gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/126672"} "Ashton Eaton"] " had retired after Rio, but the silver medallist behind him, France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125947"} "Kevin Mayer"] " was back and had set an impressive world record in 2018, with 9,126 points. Mayer had struggled in 2019-21 with injuries, however, and Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/143364"} "Niklas Kaul"] " had won the 2019 World Championship. The favorite in Tokyo was likely the Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/122729"} "Damian Warner"] ", who had won the invitational Götzis Meeting earlier in 2021, just missing the 9,000 barrier as he scored 8,995 to win."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Warner left no doubt of his intentions in the first phases, running 10.12 in the 100 metres to equal the all-time decathlon best, which he held, and then jumped 8.24 in the long jump, a mark that would have won bronze in the open long jump in Tokyo. He had a comfortable lead, as Mayer had run only 10.68 and Kaul was injured and would not finish."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Warner finished the first day with 4,722 points, leading Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/140714"} "Ashley Moloney"] " by 81 points, with Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/141491"} "Pierce LePage"] " in third. Mayer was in fifth, but trailing Warner by almost 400 points."] "\n\n" [:p {} "On the second day, Warner opened with 13.46 in the high hurdles, extending his lead. He then threw 48.67 in the discus, and the gold seemed secure, as long he could clear a height in the pole vault. He did so, recording 4.90 to equal his PR and led by 221 points. Mayer won the vault with 5.20 to move closer to the podium. Behind Warner the battle for medals was between Moloney, Mayer, LePage, and American " [:a {:href "/athletes/147328"} "Garrett Scantling"] ". Mayer improved his position, moving into second after the javelin, in which he threw a PR of 73.09."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The gold was settled as the 1,500 started but the fight for the medals was furious. Moloney needed to beat Mayer by 11 seconds to take silver, but he was not a strong 1,500 runner, and it was not certain he could stay ahead of Scantling for bronze. Moloney was paced by his teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/136545"} "Cedric Dubler"] " and Moloney ran a PR 4:39.19 to secure bronze as Mayer held on for his second consecutive silver medal, and Scantling finished in the dreaded fourth position."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Warner needed to run under 4:34 to reach 9,000 points, much faster than he had run in May at Götzis, but he did it, recording 4:31.08 to get to 9,018 points and the gold medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1440"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122729"} "Damian Warner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "9018"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1966"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125947"} "Kévin Mayer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.co